From 6f9733eb061fd81d05abeb2895912abd62cabd2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <enrico.bartky@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 16:08:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] paint: render CSS box-shadow (outset) for block and inline
 boxes
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

box-shadow was stored on the computed style but never painted — only text-shadow
was. Implement outset box-shadow: a zero-blur layer is a solid fill behind the
element's border box (offset + spread); a blurred layer is approximated by a stack
of concentric solid fills whose cumulative SrcOver coverage matches the Gaussian
(std-dev blur/2) cumulative distribution across the shape edge. Emitted before the
background in both paint paths (PaintFragmentBackgroundPhase for in-flow blocks;
EmitInlineBoxBackgroundAndBorder for inline boxes, one per line fragment); rounded
boxes clip the shadow to the border radius grown by the spread. inset layers are
not yet modelled.

Fixes WPT css/css-view-transitions/inline-child-with-overflow-shadow (inline span
with a sharp offset shadow) and renders blurred shadows within ~99.7% of Chromium.
